# .privacy-allowlist — file paths that skip PII scanning.
# One path per line: exact-path OR directory-prefix match (NOT substring — a sibling like
# foo.sh.bak does NOT inherit foo.sh's allowance). Matched against each diff's `+++ b/<path>`.
# Use sparingly — prefer fixing the content.
# Lines starting with # are comments.
# Examples:
#   docs/kdd/P731.md
#   supabase/migrations/20260410090000_fix_seal_denormalize_regression.sql

# Privacy audit scripts contain intentional pattern definitions and test fixtures
scripts/audit-privacy.sh
scripts/test-audit-privacy.sh

# Generated byte-identical mirrors of already-scanned canonical public skills.
# Canonical sources under .claude/commands/slava/ remain subject to the privacy gate.
.agents/skills
